  "proof_summary": "Retain the entire original proof that the component-one degeneracy pushforward of the level-N0*p Hecke operator at prime p equals p times the component-zero degeneracy pushforward, for every nonzero N0 and prime p and every y in JZero(N0*p). No coprimality restriction between N0 and p is added. Remove the obsolete minus-simp numerator and eta-coefficient entries, replace the one deprecated if_pos use with ite_eq_left and haveI for the proposition Fact p.Prime with have, and print the actual final solution recursive axiom closure. The original divisor self-correspondence, ramification and inertia-degree sum, beta-map degree-p identity and Pic0 descent proofs are all retained. Both source/card checks passed without warnings; the final solution actually printed exactly STANDARD3.",
